    <entry>
        <title>Bat Party Massacre</title>
        <author>
            <name>Sophie Wheldon</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://skullbuns.com/bat-party-massacre.html"/>
        <id>https://skullbuns.com/bat-party-massacre.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/ToZxqI.png" medium="image" />
            <category term="Godot"/>
            <category term="Game Jam"/>

        <updated>2025-12-15T14:25:31+00:00</updated>
            <summary>
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/ToZxqI.png" alt="" />
                    BPM was my first 3D game and an entry to a Vaporwave themed game jam. It is playable on itch.io&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/ToZxqI.png" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p></p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>Overview/Goal</h2>
<p>BPM was my first 3D game and an entry to a Vaporwave themed game jam. It is <a href="https://skullbuns.itch.io/bat-party-massacre">playable on itch.io</a> </p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>BAT PARTY MASSACRE</strong> is a first-person puzzle game where you play as a hyper-intelligent bat. You prey on humans during the night, sucking their blood and turning them into mindless drones. To achieve this, you are tasked with finding a path to a new target each night with clever tactics such as unlocking doors, breaking obstacles and scaring them. - Bat Party Massacre page</p>
</blockquote>
<h2>Media/Gallery</h2>
<div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-is-empty="false" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="3">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/sgmXah.png" data-size="954x547"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/sgmXah-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="440"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/J1uXEf.png" data-size="953x533"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/J1uXEf-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="430"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/WMmaKF.png" data-size="956x536"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/WMmaKF-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="431"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/3zxGjP.png" data-size="961x538"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/3zxGjP-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="430"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/oT1n86.png" data-size="957x539"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/oT1n86-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="433"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<h2>Contribution</h2>
<p> </p>
<h3>Tools used</h3>
<ul>
<li>Godot Engine
<ul>
<li>GDScript (Programming)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Krita (2D Graphics)</li>
<li>Blender (3D Models)</li>
</ul>
<h3>My Role</h3>
<p>I created the game mostly solo, from concept to production.</p>
<ul>
<li>I experimented with shaders using Godot's GLSL inspired shading language to create the ocean grid &amp; wave vertex movement.</li>
<li>I began learning and using hard-surface modelling for my games through free online tutorials</li>
<li>I ensured the game stuck to its Vaporwave art direction</li>
<li>I programmed the bats controls, a rudimentary dialogue system and the interactions between picking things up and the world/characters.</li>
</ul>
<p>I did get help with playtesting and voice-acting from friends,</p>
<h2>Reflection</h2>
<p>I am glad I pushed myself to finally make a 3D Game. It had its own new challenges but the end result.</p>
<p><a href="https://itch.io/jam/vaporwave-love-game-jam/rate/2920127">Feedback on the jam page</a> was very positive, with the most common approval being in how the theme/aethstetic was done.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
            ]]>
        </content>
    </entry>
