        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/fyXV45-2.png" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p></p>
<h2></h2>
<h2>Overview/Goal</h2>
<p>This game was originally made in only 3 days for the <a href="https://itch.io/jam/cozy-fall-jam-2023">Cozy Fall Jam 2023</a> game jam. it is extremely simple in terms of gameplay, as my 2 focuses for this game jam was to make a game that was easy to pick up and for it to have a polished UI and UX.</p>
<h2>Media/Gallery</h2>
<div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-is-empty="false" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="3">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/Screenshot-2025-12-15-155702.png" data-size="1145x646"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/Screenshot-2025-12-15-155702-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="433"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/Screenshot-2025-12-15-155717.png" data-size="1143x644"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/Screenshot-2025-12-15-155717-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="433"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/pausemenu.png" data-size="1152x644"><img loading="lazy" src="https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/3/gallery/pausemenu-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="429"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<h2>Contribution</h2>
<h3>Tools used</h3>
<ul>
<li>Godot Engine
<ul>
<li>GDScript (Scripting)</li>
<li>Godot Shader Language (GLSL-like shader programming)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Trello (Task Management)</li>
</ul>
<h3>My Role</h3>
<p>I was the main designer and programmer on the game. I worked in a trio on this project, interacting with our musician to make a game with an adapative soundtrack and our playtester to improve iteratively on the games mechanics, UI and aethstetics.</p>
<h3></h3>
<h2>Reflection</h2>
<p>ASWTMP, out of all my games, is the one I find myself playing the most. Players don't have to worry about strategy or tactics like other games, but it is still fun to try and get a new high score. Its menues are simple, it's vector graphics are clean and unique and I'm proud of the game our team managed to get out.</p>
